<title>GREECE: GREEK/BUND GAP WIDENS TO 338BPS FROM FRIDAY'S 336.</title>
<headline>GREEK/BUND GAP WIDENS TO 338BPS FROM FRIDAY'S 336.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The spread between Greece's</p>
<p>10-year bond and bunds widened to 338 basis points today from</p>
<p>336 basis points on Friday on the back of a higher cost of carry</p>
<p>after Greek short-term rates spiked on a liquidity squeeze.</p>
<p>		 CPN     MATURITY    YIELDS   SPREADS  PREVIOUS</p>
<p>								    SPREADS</p>
<p>   GREECE    8.80%   25JUN07	9.12%</p>
<p>   GERMANY   6.0%    04JUL07	5.74%    338	336 BPS</p>
<p>   FRANCE    5.5%    25APR07	5.66%    346	345 BPS</p>
<p>   ITALY     6.75%   01FEB07	6.94%    218	214 BPS</p>
<p>   PORTUGAL  6.63%   23FEB07	6.38%    274	273 BPS</p>
<p>   SPAIN     7.35%   31MAR07	6.40%    272	271 BPS</p>
<p>   UK	  7.25%   07DEC07	7.30%    182	182 BPS</p>
<p>   US	  6.63%   15MAY07	6.48%    264	261 BPS</p>
<p>All yields are annualised and based on bid prices at 1424</p>
<p>GMT.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
